msgid "Apache Kafka reference guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This reference guide demonstrates how your Quarkus application can utilize "
"Quarkus Messaging to interact with Apache Kafka."
msgstr ""

msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://kafka.apache.org[Apache Kafka] is a popular open-source distributed "
"event streaming platform.\n"
"It is used commonly for high-performance data pipelines, streaming "
"analytics, data integration, and mission-critical applications.\n"
"Similar to a message queue, or an enterprise messaging platform, it lets you:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*publish* (write) and *subscribe* to (read) streams of events, called "
"_records_."
msgstr ""

msgid "*store* streams of records durably and reliably inside _topics_."
msgstr ""

msgid "*process* streams of records as they occur or retrospectively."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"And all this functionality is provided in a distributed, highly scalable, "
"elastic, fault-tolerant, and secure manner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Extension for Apache Kafka"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides support for Apache Kafka through https://smallrye.io/"
"smallrye-reactive-messaging/[SmallRye Reactive Messaging] framework.\n"
"Based on Eclipse MicroProfile Reactive Messaging specification 2.0, it "
"proposes a flexible programming model bridging CDI and event-driven."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide provides an in-depth look on Apache Kafka and SmallRye Reactive "
"Messaging framework.\n"
"For a quick start take a look at xref:kafka-getting-started.adoc[Getting "
"Started to Quarkus Messaging with Apache Kafka]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can add the `messaging-kafka` extension to your project by running the "
"following command in your project base directory:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This will add the following to your build file:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The extension includes `kafka-clients` version 4.1.1 as a transitive "
"dependency and is compatible with Kafka brokers version 2.x and above."
msgstr ""

